\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The historical Boolean API implements a semi-open even-odd ray rule, whose
boundary points can belong to either parity. The new explicit location separates
exact boundary membership from that ownership convention. A straddling edge
crosses the rightward ray according to an exact orientation sign of the stored
finite binary64 coordinates, avoiding an overflowing or cancelling intersection
quotient. This classifies a closed path’s even-odd fill; it does not certify
polygon simplicity. The original concave chevron and double-increment query grid
remain. No external dataset is needed.

$$ \mathrm{inside}=\bigoplus_i\left(\mathrm{straddles}_i\ \land\ x_{query}<x_{intersection,i}\right). $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/point_in_polygon_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <datamunge/geometry/point_in_polygon.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t =
        dm::geometry::point_in_polygon_trace({1, 1},
                                             {{0, 0}, {2, 0}, {2, 2}, {0, 2}});
    std::print("\n| previous vertex | current vertex | actual y-straddle | exact " "orientation(current,previous,query) | boundary | toggled | parity after |\n| ---: | ---: | " "--- | ---: | --- | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.edges)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.previous,
                   r.current, r.straddles, r.orientation, r.boundary, r.toggled,
                   r.inside_after);

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual tested closed edges\n{}", t.edges.size()));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual accumulated ray parity\ninside={}", t.inside));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual separate boundary flag\n{}",
                       t.location == dm::geometry::PolygonLocation::Boundary));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/point_in_polygon_tiny.svg");
}
```
